{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/daemon/supervisor.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T06:09:59.609721Z","id":"4b25efefdb8879b92e60af452d87195b3e784ffeadb601994b4c655c5aeec0ba","body":{"detail":"_stopStale sends SIGTERM (then SIGKILL) to daemon.json's pid when PidKiller.alive says it exists. The supervisor deletes daemon.json when its own child exits (_forgetDaemonJson), so the file outlives its daemon only when the app itself was killed while the daemon kept running, or the daemon was killed while the app was not running. In that window the PID can be reused: on macOS by any process of the same user, which would be signalled. On Android, other apps' processes are hidden from /proc and cannot be signalled, so only this app's own processes are exposed.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":380},"end":{"line":388},"content_hash":"be7c02039e5707018cc658260314b796d0675412d387bb79b20ac880106a6017"},"suggested_fix":"Before signalling, confirm the process is the daemon: GET /healthz on daemon.json's port and compare its pid, or compare the process's executable (/proc/<pid>/exe on Android, `ps -o comm= -p <pid>` on macOS) with the located clax; signal only a match or an unanswering process whose executable is clax.","summary":"The stale-daemon stop signals whatever process holds the PID daemon.json names, without checking it is clax","tags":["risk","daemon","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/daemon/process.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T06:09:59.609799Z","id":"ac797ec904426eabec665d503877fd905235f8de66f0dfdd2808f687b681b615","body":{"detail":"`clax serve --foreground` logs through tracing_subscriber::fmt() (crates/clax-cli/src/commands/serve.rs), which writes to stdout; IoProcessStarter drains stdout and drops it. The tail that Failed carries (supervisor.dart _keepTail) therefore has what reaches stderr: panics and the `Error: …` a failing main prints, but not warnings such as a port fallback or a store problem logged before exit.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":50},"end":{"line":51},"content_hash":"16f00d39642324b163ad4aca873c5560bbf4760cd5701420e8ff23bdff58086f"},"suggested_fix":"Either keep a tail of stdout too (a second ring, or both streams merged into the one the Failed state shows), or have serve log to stderr when started by the app.","summary":"The daemon's log lines go to stdout, which is discarded, so the Failed screen's tail holds only stderr","tags":["daemon","diagnostics","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/daemon/supervisor.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T06:09:59.609845Z","id":"0a396b836e2eabf84523484ac0b23fae390079d9ba8db53cff0963dc1b20e7ed","body":{"detail":"Each such start takes the 15 s health limit plus its backoff (supervisor.dart healthLimit, backoff), so failed starts land at least 15 s apart and at most four fall within the 60 s failWindow; the five-in-sixty rule (spec §3.1 'Death') never trips. The person sees Starting/Restarting indefinitely instead of the error screen with Restart and the stderr tail. A daemon that exits at once does reach Failed (test 'a waiter of ensureUp gets the failure').","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":250},"end":{"line":265},"content_hash":"e6bd7db611f075e9ef9b14dc7ca65b4acc50cc05aa1001a8b2908cd69d1df139"},"suggested_fix":"Count consecutive failed starts separately (for example, Failed after three health timeouts in a row), or measure the failure window from the start of each attempt rather than its end.","summary":"A daemon that starts but never answers /healthz restarts forever and never reaches Failed","tags":["daemon","spec-gap","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/daemon/supervisor.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T06:09:59.609880Z","id":"9fbb9e0347073d4aa5b9dac180a1b65cf8102889079488a643c3dad3f44ba323","body":{"detail":"The daemon writes daemon.json only after Store::open_reporting returns (crates/clax-server/src/daemon.rs serve), and while it opens it reports progress in starting.json; the CLI's own spawn moves its deadline on while that progress advances (crates/clax-cli/src/client.rs Client::spawn, StartWatch). The app's supervisor uses a fixed 15 s (spec §3.1 'Up'), so a migration or audit backfill longer than that is SIGKILLed mid-open and retried from the start. A phone's fresh home opens well within it; a long-lived home after an upgrade may not.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":129},"end":{"line":129},"content_hash":"7ec891da1b7af5eb42fb9145ba1e3da4a35eed55d565d7dab7e835e3302c12ad"},"suggested_fix":"Extend the deadline while <home>/starting.json names the started PID and its heartbeat_at advances, as Client::spawn does.","summary":"The fixed 15 s health limit ignores starting.json, so a slow first open of a large home counts as a failed start and is killed","tags":["daemon","spec-gap","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/daemon/supervisor.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T06:16:04.784402Z","id":"9bf0cf6ed8a5409ed546f3838e8d492c5db2621aa223e935e272901aff79bb21","body":{"detail":"The Debug macOS build is not sandboxed (apps/clax_app/macos/Runner/DebugProfile.entitlements has no com.apple.security.app-sandbox), so IoPidKiller can signal any process of the user. daemon.json outlives its daemon whenever the daemon dies without a graceful shutdown (it removes the file only on a clean exit, crates/clax-server/src/daemon.rs:740-741): a SIGKILL, a crash, power loss. After a reboot PIDs are handed out again from low numbers, so the next launch is the likeliest moment for daemon.json's PID to belong to another process, which then gets SIGTERM and, 3 s later, SIGKILL. The check is cheap: /healthz already answers the daemon's own pid (crates/clax-server/src/routes/health.rs). Signal only when GET /healthz on daemon.json's port answers with daemon.json's pid. A live PID that does not answer is left alone: the new daemon rewrites daemon.json, and the old daemon's stale watcher exits within one check interval once it sees another live PID there (crates/clax-server/src/daemon.rs:627-635). The new daemon takes another port if the old one still holds the kept one. Add a test where alive(pid) is true but health answers another pid (or nothing): no signal is sent.","kind":"comment","references":"4b25efefdb8879b92e60af452d87195b3e784ffeadb601994b4c655c5aeec0ba","span":{"start":{"line":380},"end":{"line":388},"content_hash":"be7c02039e5707018cc658260314b796d0675412d387bb79b20ac880106a6017"},"summary":"Review: fix in this task, before the supervisor is wired into the app","tags":["review","daemon","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/daemon/supervisor.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T06:16:04.784516Z","id":"eb435709da34a921e9cd885c3bc3559e3920d2b5d5dd5cf20b4df3c2c4b30253","body":{"detail":"Spec §3.1 'Death' and §7 'Errors' (the 'Daemon exits' row) show the error screen (Restart, stderr tail) when the daemon cannot stay up; the screen is driven by Failed, and Failed is never reached by a daemon that hangs before /healthz. Together with 9fbb9e03, a store open that takes longer than 15 s is SIGKILLed and retried every ~20 s forever behind a spinner. Count consecutive starts that never reached Up and go Failed after three in a row (about 46 s), keeping five-in-sixty for exits after Up. Test: health.answers = false, advance 15 s + backoff three times, expect Failed with the 'did not answer /healthz' reason; a start that does reach Up resets the count.","kind":"comment","references":"0a396b836e2eabf84523484ac0b23fae390079d9ba8db53cff0963dc1b20e7ed","span":{"start":{"line":250},"end":{"line":265},"content_hash":"e6bd7db611f075e9ef9b14dc7ca65b4acc50cc05aa1001a8b2908cd69d1df139"},"summary":"Review: cap it in this task; Failed is the supervisor's contract with the error screen","tags":["review","daemon","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/daemon/supervisor.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T06:16:04.784564Z","id":"0b5932c61b5956e93dc7ca6f20eb2e18680efd86b4c0a2a38dd45236de7e7649","body":{"detail":"The supervisor restarts an exited daemon at once whether or not the app is in the foreground (supervisor.dart _loop). On Android 12+, the phantom process killer kills a cached app's children, and each restart spawns another child while the app is still in the background; five kills within 60 s reach Failed. onResume returns early when _loopDone is null (line 198), which is the case after Failed, so the person comes back to the error screen though nothing is wrong and a plain start would succeed. The same happens on Android 12-13 without the cached-apps freezer, where the Dart isolate keeps running in the background. Spec §3.1 'Resume' expects resume to bring a killed daemon back.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":193},"end":{"line":210},"content_hash":"1e1639c708ee9621c677b3a82b329c03cc95087a8069b51fecec74c5a8a21f3d"},"suggested_fix":"Have onResume start afresh from Failed (as ensureUp does, clearing the exit history), or add an onPause that stops counting exits (and restarting) until resume. Test: five exits, Failed, then onResume -> Starting -> Up.","summary":"Exits while the app is in the background count toward Failed, and onResume does nothing once Failed","tags":["review","daemon","android","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/daemon/supervisor.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T06:16:04.784608Z","id":"048963d063f0c33cd64ca408be08149ed6bd19b75522cc1357a6e9ec685270d7","body":{"detail":"onResume kills the daemon after a single HttpHealthProbe failure (2 s timeout, apps/clax_app/lib/daemon/health.dart:13). Right after the app is unfrozen the daemon can be slow to answer; killing it costs a restart and a WebView reload. SQLite's WAL makes the kill safe, so this is cost, not damage.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":204},"end":{"line":209},"content_hash":"29cb87b2e2f00a48f0365185f449b16b13a238f3369f6a02b64d2ff51fb2a68b"},"suggested_fix":"Probe a second time (or check _proc's exit first, which is exact for a dead child) before killing.","summary":"One failed 2 s probe on resume SIGKILLs a daemon that may only be slow to wake","tags":["review","daemon","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/daemon/supervisor.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T06:20:33.048194Z","id":"e0866744a5dc24d4415a5953c46b6e7f2c675999ca16b98688ca7b64aa8fde0c","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"_stopStale signals only when HealthProbe.pid on daemon.json's port answers daemon.json's pid. Tests 'a live PID that /healthz does not answer as is left alone' (unit) and 'a live process that daemon.json names but that is not the daemon is left alone' (real clax, a live /bin/sleep named in daemon.json survives) pass; CLAX_TEST_BIN=$(tool/test-bin.sh) flutter test test/daemon (apps/clax_app): 31 passed","supersedes":"4b25efefdb8879b92e60af452d87195b3e784ffeadb601994b4c655c5aeec0ba","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/daemon/supervisor.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T06:20:33.048395Z","id":"7a45efb82e4c9ea6fd083c16dca33b2de1c01471d0c3f5f3200c54a891d3799a","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"startFailAfter = 3: three starts in a row that never come up is Failed; a start that reaches Up resets the count. Tests 'three starts in a row that never come up is Failed' and 'a start that comes up resets the count of starts that did not' pass; CLAX_TEST_BIN=$(tool/test-bin.sh) flutter test test/daemon (apps/clax_app): 31 passed","supersedes":"0a396b836e2eabf84523484ac0b23fae390079d9ba8db53cff0963dc1b20e7ed","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/daemon/process.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T06:20:33.048530Z","id":"a8f47ccec66a09e5bde3a7ec7bce30c9c35d3f356e7f3c2cd9ef7beeb8097314","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"RunningProcess exposes stdout; the supervisor keeps one tail of stdout and stderr lines as they arrive. Test 'backoff grows ... Failed with the stderr tail' asserts a stdout line in Failed.stderrTail; CLAX_TEST_BIN=$(tool/test-bin.sh) flutter test test/daemon (apps/clax_app): 31 passed","supersedes":"ac797ec904426eabec665d503877fd905235f8de66f0dfdd2808f687b681b615","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/daemon/supervisor.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T06:20:33.048659Z","id":"ae92755d7d23c46436e64c7e5812673dbe5005ab818d5d70bd734b488f091141","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"onResume starts afresh from Failed (exit history cleared), and still does nothing after stop. Tests 'onResume starts afresh once Failed' (Failed -> Starting -> Up) and 'onResume after stop does nothing' pass; CLAX_TEST_BIN=$(tool/test-bin.sh) flutter test test/daemon (apps/clax_app): 31 passed","supersedes":"0b5932c61b5956e93dc7ca6f20eb2e18680efd86b4c0a2a38dd45236de7e7649","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/daemon/supervisor.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T06:20:33.048787Z","id":"4563ce4ec8ed02e0996e301f5c23639137ced7d17abee01c46c5ea803452b731","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"onResume probes /healthz a second time before killing. Test 'onResume probes again before restarting a daemon slow to answer' (one failed probe, no kill) passes, and 'onResume restarts a dead daemon and leaves a live one' still kills after two; CLAX_TEST_BIN=$(tool/test-bin.sh) flutter test test/daemon (apps/clax_app): 31 passed","supersedes":"048963d063f0c33cd64ca408be08149ed6bd19b75522cc1357a6e9ec685270d7","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/daemon/daemon_key.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T02:22:28.235285Z","id":"695570708ca8695e530f5ead6a034acc702d1eda12de22adcb8a568002f162a5","body":{"detail":"DaemonKey.write calls DaemonSupervisor.restart when the saved key changes, so the daemon reads ANTHROPIC_API_KEY again. The runtime sees Starting then Up (no Failed), which re-registers the session; an open app reconnects, but a running agent change's daemon calls in the gap fail and its recovery reruns it. A runtime key-set route on the daemon would avoid the restart. Key changes are rare, so the restart was the simpler choice.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":6},"end":{"line":21},"content_hash":"0b01d3993e6ce841ebdf24abc16a2e22d4f319ce5109978d9113bfea817748fc"},"summary":"Saving a new API key in Settings restarts the daemon, cutting an open app's streams and any change in flight","tags":["revisit:people change keys while changes run","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/daemon/supervisor.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T03:19:20.578716Z","id":"9fb07128bea8daf4e425ddee69755dc659be6626a68aa3842dc06cdd206597dd","body":{"detail":"The owner and events cookies (crates/clax-server/src/identity.rs, crates/clax-server/src/auth.rs events_cookie_value) hold a SHA-256 of the token and are set HttpOnly with SameSite=Lax or Strict (probe: GET /api/token with the key cookie answered Set-Cookie clax_owner_<port>=<hex>; Path=/api; HttpOnly; SameSite=Lax). clax_key_<port> holds the token itself, and webview_flutter's setCookie (webview_flutter_android 4.14.1 android_webview_cookie_manager.dart:60-63 writes only name=value; path=) sets neither HttpOnly nor SameSite, so document.cookie on the shell's origin reads the bearer token and it is stored in clear in the WebView cookie database. Every script on http://127.0.0.1:<port> today is the shell's own (content, /_blob/ and raw files there are CSP-sandboxed), and the shell fetches the token anyway, so nothing reads it that could not already; a derived value (as the owner cookie) checked by has_key_cookie would keep the token out of the cookie store.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":74},"end":{"line":84},"content_hash":"27834f7e2584e1715bd610eba23eb67764866efceaa22c7b263f41fba233351a"},"summary":"The key cookie carries the raw token, readable by script and without SameSite","tags":["review","security","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/daemon/supervisor.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T03:30:27.959619Z","id":"5708f5731329e91494046053cd6ddcc3b322ab2dc96e74e834e1f92f59d6ee00","body":{"detail":"Checked: nothing in web/shell, web/bridge or crates reads clax_key_<port> from script (grep -rln clax_key web/ crates/: only crates/clax-server/src/auth.rs and its test). HttpOnly and SameSite: webview_flutter_android 4.14.1 lib/src/android_webview_cookie_manager.dart:60-63 builds the Set-Cookie value itself as '<name>=<value>; path=<path>' (the path check rejects ';', the name and value are percent-encoded), so no attribute can be added; webview_flutter_wkwebview 3.27.0 lib/src/webkit_webview_cookie_manager.dart:49-64 passes only name, value, domain and path to HTTPCookie, and its HttpCookiePropertyKey has no HttpOnly key (sameSitePolicy exists but is not reachable through WebViewCookie). Setting either needs the platform cookie APIs below webview_flutter (a direct dependency on webview_flutter_android's generated android.webkit bindings and on WKHTTPCookieStore), which this app does not take today. A derived value (as clax_owner_<port>) would pass the same gate (crates/clax-server/src/auth.rs require_credential), and the shell origin's GET /api/token answers the token to whoever holds it, so a script on http://127.0.0.1:<port> that reads the cookie could fetch the token either way; the token is also in <support>/clax-home/daemon.json in the same app-private storage as the WebView cookie database. Without SameSite, WKWebView sends the cookie on cross-site requests (an <id>.localhost frame posting to 127.0.0.1): the gate passes, but every write route still asks the bearer token or the owner cookie, which is SameSite. Proposal: close as wontfix; reopen if a script not the shell's ever runs on the daemon's own origin.","kind":"comment","references":"9fb07128bea8daf4e425ddee69755dc659be6626a68aa3842dc06cdd206597dd","summary":"No script reads the key cookie, but webview_flutter cannot set HttpOnly or SameSite on either platform, and a derived value would hide nothing: proposed to close as wontfix","tags":["security","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/daemon/supervisor.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T12:12:39.358622Z","id":"fb5494d8c4f41c9a06df7cb6c1bef283c2e86949150d3a84ff49978c77c5adf7","body":{"kind":"resolve","summary":"Owner decision (2026-10-14), answering whether to close as won't-fix: \"Won't fix\". webview_flutter cannot set HttpOnly or SameSite on either platform; the key cookie is host-only on 127.0.0.1 and never reaches artifact origins, and no page script reads it.","supersedes":"9fb07128bea8daf4e425ddee69755dc659be6626a68aa3842dc06cdd206597dd","tags":["reason:wontfix","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/daemon/supervisor.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T05:09:26.692879Z","id":"c58da88f53981a29558fed6a23ad5feab41a842775e2cf2c14cedb3d9158ffab","body":{"detail":"_putKey sends the saved key once per Up and once per keyChanged; SampleKeyPort.put answering false (or throwing) is ignored. On iOS a put lost to a transient loopback error leaves the daemon's KeySlot empty, so pages' sample() answers no_key though a key is saved.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":586},"end":{"line":608},"content_hash":"929b2ccba627cc456c47d8d0ec8a2e25542996cd2c4b735b5e8558d38f695ce1"},"summary":"A key put that fails is not retried: sample() stays off on an in-process daemon until the next key change or restart","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/daemon/daemon_key.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T05:09:26.693248Z","id":"2e3ba559d3425758db02a4a5c2f6b2a02a984e8af020a4fdde4ec7e59fd4b641","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"695570708ca8695e530f5ead6a034acc702d1eda12de22adcb8a568002f162a5","summary":"With DaemonHost.inProcess (iOS) a saved key no longer restarts the daemon: DaemonKey.onChanged is DaemonSupervisor.keyChanged, which puts the key over PUT /api/sample/key (test/daemon/in_process_test.dart, 'keyChanged while up puts the new key and starts nothing'). Android and the Mac still restart the child daemon, so this thread stays open for them.","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/daemon/daemon_key.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T21:56:50.357917Z","id":"de735ce4651425133ebc441646f4fefd66eadf6646a4c557f2ca6b3d113d30fa","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"No daemon restarts on a key change any more: lib/daemon/daemon_key.dart's DaemonKey is now a typedef of NotifyingSecureKey (apps/clax_app/lib/platform/secure_key.dart), whose onChanged in lib/main.dart is CoreHost.keyChanged, which puts the key into the open core (PUT /api/sample/key) and starts nothing. bazelisk test //apps/clax_app:platform_secure_key_test: 11 passed ('a saved or removed key is reported; the same key is not').","supersedes":"695570708ca8695e530f5ead6a034acc702d1eda12de22adcb8a568002f162a5","tags":["reason:obsolete","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/daemon/supervisor.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T21:56:50.417739Z","id":"4cb5cdc66cd48df020624e0775dcd9d4c1278f3c23c3abcc400cb8ead9e14fae","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"apps/clax_app/lib/daemon/supervisor.dart is deleted: the app opens the embedded core through CoreHost, which has no health limit and hears the core's migration progress (CoreOpening) until it is ready.","supersedes":"9fbb9e0347073d4aa5b9dac180a1b65cf8102889079488a643c3dad3f44ba323","tags":["reason:obsolete","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/daemon/supervisor.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T21:56:50.477864Z","id":"f7ad5dd3239287c7d37ed15e49a96f15df3e235ddcc452a29f6b8bf5e7f912e6","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"apps/clax_app/lib/daemon/supervisor.dart is deleted. CoreHost._put (apps/clax_app/lib/core/core_host.dart:190-213) does not retry a failed put either; that risk is recorded on core_host.dart.","supersedes":"c58da88f53981a29558fed6a23ad5feab41a842775e2cf2c14cedb3d9158ffab","tags":["reason:obsolete","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/daemon/clock.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T21:56:50.703933Z","id":"b8833ada52071fa3c340a33511bb3e764b670b5d9b38e24c3df655cbf62977b6","body":{"detail":"The clock is apps/clax_app/lib/platform/clock.dart and the key apps/clax_app/lib/platform/secure_key.dart's NotifyingSecureKey. lib/daemon/clock.dart re-exports the clock for lib/app.dart:47, lib/queue/isolate_client.dart, lib/queue/worker_main.dart and lib/queue/host.dart; lib/daemon/daemon_key.dart keeps DaemonKey as a typedef for lib/main.dart:23 and :187. HomeKeeper.daemonUp (lib/home/home_keeper.dart:93), called from lib/app.dart:1552, still carries the daemon's name.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1},"end":{"line":5},"content_hash":"c6fdd2f759e295f5059d6e1aa32807a8e780ec0f3b9a974c1058ec6befd88c44"},"suggested_fix":"Point those imports at lib/platform/, use NotifyingSecureKey in main.dart, rename daemonUp to coreReady, then delete lib/daemon/.","summary":"lib/daemon/clock.dart and lib/daemon/daemon_key.dart are kept only as shims for lib/app.dart, lib/main.dart and lib/queue/","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/daemon/clock.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T22:17:14.027624Z","id":"118c21da26bfa84cbb59be510a55e50765d12ea6441afdea2277883c7258a971","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"Fixed: lib/app.dart, lib/main.dart and lib/queue/ import lib/platform/clock.dart and NotifyingSecureKey directly, and lib/daemon/ is deleted; bazelisk test //apps/clax_app:dart_analyze passes.","supersedes":"b8833ada52071fa3c340a33511bb3e764b670b5d9b38e24c3df655cbf62977b6","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
